id: pm-github-vhi6
title: Bound coverage aggregation memory and compare default-heap CI behavior
description: "During the PR #122 privacy-scope regression work, an identity-isolated npm release:check completed 587/587 tests with zero failures, skips or cancellations, then c8 report aggregation exhausted Node's default 4 GiB heap. Native coverage receipts occupied approximately 2.9 GiB. The security fix is being validated with NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=12288 and unchanged source inventory and four 100-percent thresholds. Compare default-heap CI behavior, investigate bounded report aggregation or documented resource requirements, and retain complete authored-source and real CLI coverage. Earlier local heap-exhaustion observations also appear in pm-github-fmrf; this task tracks current default-heap acceptance separately from the scope fix in pm-github-wrmt."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: coverage,follow-up,gates
